From b0ee0929a1fc12c121f5604eda244a377ce17874 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: icanc0 <ai7@vincentxie.net>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:57:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] P10: extract OnPgmRun dispatch to CLI::RunKicadCliDispatch;
 daemon uses it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two refactor threads land together:

1. kicad/kicad_cli.cpp — moves the argparse-construction + subcommand
   lookup + Perform call out of PGM_KICAD::OnPgmRun into a new file-
   external CLI::RunKicadCliDispatch(argc, argv). OnPgmRun now just
   forwards to it with m_argcUtf8/m_argvUtf8. Same behavior, one entry
   point.

2. kicad/cli/command_daemon.cpp — handleOneClient() now:
     - dup2()s stdout/stderr into a pipe pair,
     - chdir()s to the request's cwd (so relative -o and input paths
       resolve where the client expected),
     - calls RunKicadCliDispatch(argc, argv),
     - restores stdio, drains the pipes, restores cwd,
     - packages exit code + captured stdout + captured stderr into the
       wire-protocol response.

3. New kicad/cli/dispatch.h declares the extern for anyone else who
   needs to dispatch (future in-process test hooks etc.).

With this, a client that sends 'pcb export svg -l F.Cu board.kicad_pcb'
into the socket gets a real SVG on disk and the daemon's captured
stdout back — the whole point of the daemon. Syntax-checks clean under
g++ -fsyntax-only -std=c++20. End-to-end run needs a full kicad build,
which is still deferred (dep-chase blocker in benchmarks/00-baseline).
